from connected_research_case import ResearchAuthor,present_case

a=ResearchAuthor('ai-7/22')
if 'Two 45-minute sessions.' in str(a.w):a.replace_text('Two 45-minute sessions.','Use the three-session teaching cycle above, with extra time as needed.')
present_case(a,
 headline='Use the pilot to repair the procedure before the primary study',
 purpose='Preserve pilot defects and revisions while keeping new primary evidence separate.',
 intro='A pilot is a rehearsal of the measurement and study procedure. Can the team capture records, interpret the rubric and calculate the planned result? Discovering a defect is useful development evidence. Once that evidence guides a repair, it is no longer an untouched evaluation of the final procedure. Save what failed, what changed and why, then freeze the revised method before using newly reserved primary cases.',
 contract=[['Pilot item','Complete supplied exercise contract'],['Main pilot','Five cases reveal wrong units in duration logs'],['Known defect','Unit handling is wrong; actual values and conversion direction are not supplied'],['Repair record','Preserve original log, corrected interpretation, unit definition and method version'],['Primary comparison','Use newly reserved cases after the revised method is fixed'],['Separate picture','Two reviewers score four practice answers; agree on three, disagree on one'],['Picture data role','Practice answers used for revision are excluded from final evaluation'],['Unknown evidence','No verified reference labels, disagreement cause, actual timings or final-study results']],
 ledger=[['Main pilot step','Supported action','Unsupported claim'],['Five-case pilot exposes wrong duration units','Document defect and affected measurement','Pretend the original logs were correct'],['Correct unit handling','Record expected units, actual units and conversion evidence','Invent a numerical conversion without the missing values'],['Method revised using pilot','Retain pilot as development evidence','Call revised pilot outcomes an untouched final comparison'],['Freeze revised procedure','Record new version and planned measurement boundaries','Claim version label alone proves chronology'],['New primary cases','Reserve and evaluate under the fixed revised plan','Claim primary results before running the study']],
 picture='The separate picture gives four practice answers scored by two reviewers. Three agreements out of four are 75% observed agreement; one disagreement is 25%. We are not told which answer differs, the label categories, who is right or why they disagreed. Inspect the actual scoring record and rubric before choosing a repair. Agreement does not establish correctness, and four answers do not establish long-run reliability. If these answers help revise the rubric or procedure, retain them as development evidence and keep them separate from untouched final evaluation. Adding the corrected practice cases to the final set would blur that role boundary.',
 picture_table=[['Picture quantity','Supported value or limit'],['Answers scored by both reviewers','Four'],['Agree','Three; 3/4 = 75%'],['Disagree','One; 1/4 = 25%'],['Who is correct','Not supplied; agreement is not a reference label'],['Cause of disagreement','Unknown; inspect records and rubric'],['After used for revision','Development evidence, excluded from final evaluation under this plan'],['Long-run reliability / final effect','Not established by four practice answers']],
 probes=[['Pilot audit','Checked interpretation'],['Pilot uncovers a defect','Useful evidence about procedure readiness'],['Units wrong but values absent','Do not invent a conversion or repaired timing'],['Pilot used to change method','Retain development role; do not call it untouched final evidence'],['Reviewers agree','May still share an incorrect interpretation'],['Reviewers disagree','Cause and correct label require inspection'],['Four-answer agreement is 75%','Observed agreement only, not proven long-run reliability'],['New primary study planned','No results exist until it is actually performed'],['Ambiguous cases found','Revise and check rubric; do not silently delete difficult primary cases']],
 investigation='Perform a paper readiness audit of the five-case unit defect. List the missing duration values and unit definitions rather than inventing a conversion. Propose a controlled fixture with known expected units to check the repaired logger; label it proposed, not run. Then calculate picture agreement 3/4 = 75% and disagreement 1/4 = 25%. Record which scoring details are missing and how inspecting them could guide rubric revision. Preserve the original pilot, proposed correction, revised method and separately reserved primary role. Do not recruit reviewers, claim actual timings or add corrected pilot answers to the final evaluation.',
 teacher_key='Main: preserve the five-case unit defect and correction history; values and unit direction are absent, so no numerical conversion is justified. Pilot-informed revision is development evidence. Freeze the revised method before newly reserved primary cases. Picture: three agreements and one disagreement among four practice answers gives 75% observed agreement, not correctness or long-run reliability. The disagreement cause is unknown. Corrected practice answers remain excluded from final evaluation under this plan. Independent six-case pilot with two ambiguous labels calls for inspecting ambiguity, refining scoring instructions, checking the revised procedure and fixing the plan before primary data. Preserve difficult cases and revisions; do not claim a final model effect.',
 reference='A pilot checks feasibility, capture, units, rubric and analysis before a primary study. Main five-case pilot reveals wrong duration-log units. Preserve the original defect and correction; without actual values or unit definitions, no numerical conversion can be calculated. A method revised using pilot results needs newly reserved primary cases for an untouched final comparison. Separate picture: two reviewers score four practice answers, agree on three and disagree on one. Observed agreement is 3/4 = 75%; disagreement is 25%. No reference labels or disagreement cause are supplied. Agreement does not prove correctness or long-run reliability. Inspect scoring records and clarify the rubric, retaining the pilot as development evidence. Adding corrected practice cases to final evaluation would mix roles under the stated plan. Preserve versions, test the repair on appropriate fixtures and fix the revised analysis plan before new primary outcomes. No actual timing run, reviewer study or final effect estimate is supplied.',
 independent='Explain what the two ambiguous pilot labels require before the primary study; distinguish proposed repairs from completed checks.',
 image={'type':'image','src':'/api/resource/ai-7-22-pilot-agreement','alt':'Two reviewers agree on three of four practice answers and disagree on one, giving seventy-five percent observed agreement. Agreement is not correctness or long-run reliability. These answers remain development evidence after they inform revision.','caption':'Four-answer pilot summary only. No reference labels, disagreement cause or actual reviewer recruitment is supplied.'})
